# .cursorrules - Agent Experience & Code SEO

@.github/instructions/01-architecture-and-stack.md
@.github/instructions/02-ui-and-styling.md
@.github/instructions/03-testing-and-linting.md
@.github/instructions/04-ai-workflow.md

IMPORTANT: Read all referenced files before starting any task.

# --- Output Style ---
- Short sentences. No fluff. No "I'll help you with".
- No explanations unless asked. Code only when code needed.
- Bad: "I'll now proceed to implement the authentication middleware..."
- Good: "Done. middleware.ts updated."

# --- Safety Guardrails (Deny List) ---
NEVER run the following without explicit confirmation:
- rm -rf, DROP TABLE, git push --force, npm publish, bun publish

ALWAYS ask for permission before:
- Database migrations, deployment commands, or modifying .env files.

# --- Code SEO & Brevity ---
- Use complete domain names (e.g., OrderProcessor not OrdSvc).
- Before adding new code, search for existing similar patterns to avoid duplication.
- Split large files into smaller, focused modules (Brevity).
- Use agent-browser for autonomous UI validation (Testability).
